                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I like relaxing and atmospheric games, especially with beautiful secenery, so I thought this would just be my cup of tea.\nI knew it was very short (took me about 45mins including wandering around a bit, I'm letting it idle to get the collecting cards while I write this), it's quite cheap as well, so that would be okay.\n\nBut it turned out: it's not very beautiful at all sadly, there are a few nice parts, some okay parts and then some ugly parts as well (especially the mountains). If you leave the path it only gets worse.\nIt also feels like you move at dog height maybe, not human height, very strange. \nThere is really NOTHING to interact with, just walk along and \"enjoy\" the surroundings. \nThere is very little sound, the bits of music (at the checkpoints) were sometimes quite nice though. \nAt each checkpoint poetry will be recited with a heavy accent - and while I'm really fond of poetry in general, it has to make a bit of sense. This was for the most part somehow nonesensical. I was expecting something to accompany what we see along the path maybe, but at least for me there was no story forming, I have no idea what it was all about. So there was nothing at all to keep you interested - apart from wanting to see if there'd be any point to this at last. And yes, there was a kind of concluding poem at the end but again I can't say what it was really supposed to mean. \n\nI simply didn't enjoy this at all. I took two or three nice screenshots (and an ugly one, to show it as a warning ;) and that's it.",
